From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:07:16 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] wireplumber: no pro-audio profile on the headphone-jack
 cards

The AOP-fed headphone jacks (J614s, J616s, J713) are sound cards of their
own. Their UCM HiFi profile is the whole card: the Headphones output and
the Headset Microphone input. The pro-audio profile only offers the same
PCM again as raw AUX0/AUX1 channels.

With nothing plugged in, HiFi is unavailable and pro-audio is the only
profile besides Off, so a user looking for the jack selects "Pro Audio".
WirePlumber stores that choice and keeps it over HiFi from then on, and
the jack shows up as an unnamed two-channel AUX device with no hardware
volume. Disable pro-audio on these cards (api.acp.disable-pro-audio,
matched on the card name ending in " Jack"); HiFi and Off remain.

Reported-by: saku <saku-bruh@proton.me>
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 conf/wireplumber.conf | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/conf/wireplumber.conf b/conf/wireplumber.conf
index 44ce344..4b5196f 100644
--- a/conf/wireplumber.conf
+++ b/conf/wireplumber.conf
@@ -87,6 +87,23 @@ monitor.alsa.rules = [
             }
         }
     }
+    # A headphone jack that is a card of its own (the AOP-fed jacks: macaudio
+    # "MacBook Pro J614 Jack", "MacBook Pro J616 Jack", "MacBook Air J713
+    # Jack") has one stereo output and one mono input, both described by its
+    # UCM HiFi profile. Its pro-audio profile adds nothing but raw AUX0/AUX1
+    # channels, and with nothing plugged in it is the only profile besides
+    # "Off": users looking for the jack picked it, and WirePlumber then kept
+    # it over HiFi. Leave such a card HiFi and Off only.
+    {
+        matches = [
+            { device.name = "~alsa_card.*", api.alsa.card.name = "~^Mac.* Jack$" }
+        ]
+        actions = {
+            update-props = {
+                api.acp.disable-pro-audio = true
+            }
+        }
+    }
     # J616s: the headphone jack is a card of its own (hw:AppleJack, macaudio
     # "MacBook Pro J616 Jack"), so UCM's priorities between the jack and the
     # speakers do not apply across the two cards. Its UCM ties the Headphones
